# Lab credentials — local only

Copy this file to `lab-credentials.md` **in the same directory** and fill in the values.
That filename is in `.gitignore`; this `.example` is the only one that is committed.

## Rule that keeps this file from becoming a liability

For anything that also exists in source, **the source is authoritative and this file is only a
lookup shortcut**. Record where the real value lives and when you last checked, so a stale copy
here can never be mistaken for the truth.

| What | Authoritative source | Value | Snapshot date |
|---|---|---|---|
| ARM `ubuntu` password (Bronco / non-Bronco) | `utopx: src/arm_agent_api/ArmAgentApiOS.cpp` `GetArmPassword()` | | |
| ARM user name (Bronco / non-Bronco) | same file, `GetArmUserName()` | | |
| DPU-BMC factory login | OpenBMC upstream default — already documented in `key-learnings.md`, not a secret | `admin:0penBmc` | — |
| QA-standard BMC account | team password store | | |

## Not in here

Anything personal (your own SSH keys, tokens, `~/.jenkins_env`, `~/.confluence_env`). Those stay
in their own files with mode 600 — see the global notes. This file is for **shared lab
credentials** that several skills need to quote.
